{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2156-06-09 05:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning, Ms. ___. I'm Dr. ___, one of your hospital doctors. I understand you’ve been feeling nauseous and vomited after dinner last night?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2156-06-09 05:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, that’s right. I felt sick to my stomach and threw up once. I haven’t eaten much since."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2156-06-09 05:17:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. Any chest pain, shortness of breath, or diarrhea?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2156-06-09 05:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No, no chest pain or trouble breathing. Just the nausea and some dizziness."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2156-06-09 05:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Okay. I notice you had a cold a week ago—sneezing, congestion, cough. Is that better now?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2156-06-09 05:20:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, that’s improving. My family had it too—my grandchildren and son-in-law—but no one had a fever or stomach issues."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2156-06-09 05:21:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Thanks. We also see your INR came back high at 3.8. That’s related to your warfarin. We’ll hold that for now to reduce bleeding risk."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2156-06-09 05:22:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh, I didn’t know it was that high. Should I be worried?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2156-06-09 05:23:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not at this moment. We’re monitoring it. We’ll restart warfarin once it’s safer. Your heart rhythm is still irregular, so we’re keeping you on amiodarone and metoprolol."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2156-06-09 05:24:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that makes sense. I’ve been dizzy lately, especially after dialysis."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2156-06-09 05:25:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we saw you couldn’t tolerate ultrafiltration last time. We’ve stopped your furosemide to help stabilize your blood pressure."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2156-06-09 05:26:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh, so I should stop taking that pill?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2156-06-09 05:27:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Correct, we’re discontinuing it for now. We don’t want to drop your blood pressure too low, especially with your heart rhythm issues."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2156-06-09 05:28:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. What about the nausea? Do you know what’s causing it?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2156-06-09 05:29:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Most likely, it’s viral gastroenteritis—like a stomach bug. You’ve been around sick family, and you’re immunosuppressed, so we’re watching closely."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2156-06-09 05:30:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I see. And my cough? It’s still a bit there."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2156-06-09 05:31:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We tested for flu—both A and B—and it was negative. We’ll treat your cough with guaifenesin to help loosen the mucus."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2156-06-09 05:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I can take that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2156-06-09 08:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning again. Your urine test showed an infection—Enterococcus. It’s sensitive to vancomycin, which we can use since you’re allergic to penicillin and sulfa."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2156-06-09 08:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve had this before. Is it serious?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2156-06-09 08:17:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It can be, especially with your transplant history. We’ll treat it with vancomycin during your dialysis sessions for about two weeks."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2156-06-09 08:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will I get it through my dialysis line?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2156-06-09 08:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, it’ll be given slowly during each session. We’ll also check trough levels to make sure the dose is right."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2156-06-09 12:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You just finished your first dialysis session. How are you feeling?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2156-06-09 12:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "A bit tired, but the nausea is better. No dizziness this time."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2156-06-09 12:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s great to hear. Your labs are improving—creatinine is down from 2.7 to 2.4, and your electrolytes are stable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2156-06-09 12:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my INR? Is it still high?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2156-06-09 12:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s still elevated, so we’re holding warfarin. We’ll check it again before you go home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2156-06-10 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your chest X-ray shows no pneumonia or fluid in the lungs. Just some mild, stable changes from old scarring."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2156-06-10 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So my breathing is okay?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2156-06-10 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, lungs are clear. Your heart rhythm is still irregular, but stable. We’re continuing your amiodarone and metoprolol."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2156-06-10 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my transplant kidney? I know it’s not working anymore."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2156-06-10 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s right. The biopsy showed chronic damage. We’re still discussing with your nephrologist whether removal is needed. No decision yet."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2156-06-10 09:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m worried about more infections. It’s been a long road."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2156-06-10 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I understand. We’re monitoring for CMV, BK, and EBV viruses. So far, CMV is not detected. The other results are pending."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2156-06-11 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good news—your nausea is gone, and you’re eating well. We’re planning to discharge you today."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2156-06-11 08:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s great. What do I need to do at home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2156-06-11 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Continue all your usual meds except furosemide—we’re stopping that. Hold warfarin until your INR is checked. Take guaifenesin for cough as needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2156-06-11 08:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the vancomycin?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2156-06-11 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll get five more doses during dialysis. Your kidney doctor will arrange it. Also, check your INR on ___ and call Dr. ___."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2156-06-11 08:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, doctor. I appreciate all the care."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2156-06-11 08:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Keep following up with your specialists. We’ll send all results to them. Feel better soon."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2156-06-09 05:13:00",
    "admission_end": "2156-06-11 15:42:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "The patient was admitted for nausea, vomiting, and dizziness following a recent hospitalization complicated by flash pulmonary edema and pancytopenia. She had a history of polycystic kidney disease, renal transplant with subsequent graft failure, and was on hemodialysis. Evaluation revealed viral gastroenteritis as the likely cause of gastrointestinal symptoms and a urinary tract infection due to pansensitive Enterococcus, treated with vancomycin administered during dialysis. Her atrial fibrillation remained stable on amiodarone and metoprolol, but warfarin was held due to an elevated INR of 3.8. Furosemide was discontinued to address hypotension and intolerance to ultrafiltration. A chest X-ray showed no acute cardiopulmonary findings. She improved clinically, with resolution of nausea and stable vital signs, and was discharged home with plans for continued vancomycin therapy during dialysis, INR monitoring, and follow-up with her nephrologist regarding potential transplant kidney removal.",
    "problems": [
      "Intestinal infection due to other organism, not elsewhere classified",
      "End stage renal disease",
      "Urinary tract infection, site not specified",
      "Hypertensive chronic kidney disease, unspecified, with chronic kidney disease stage V or end stage renal disease",
      "Complications of transplanted kidney",
      "Renal dialysis status",
      "Atrial fibrillation",
      "Unspecified acquired hypothyroidism",
      "Surgical operation with transplant of whole organ causing abnormal patient reaction, or later complication, without mention of misadventure at time of operation",
      "Personal history of malignant neoplasm of other parts of uterus",
      "Primary hyperparathyroidism",
      "Streptococcus infection in conditions classified elsewhere and of unspecified site, streptococcus, group D [Enterococcus]",
      "Other and unspecified hyperlipidemia",
      "Acute upper respiratory infections of unspecified site"
    ]
  }
}
